[node name="Left" type="RichTextLabel" parent="TabContainer/About 1" unique_id=1218837951]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 91.0
offset_top = 142.0
offset_right = 839.0
offset_bottom = 912.0
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/book_closed.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]TUTORIAL[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]FNAF WORLD TCG, is as its name implies, a card game that bases itself from the World of Five Nights at Freddy's  by Scott Cawthon. In this game you the player will be able to play a rather simple game of cards, against a basic AI or you can play with, or in this case against, a friend on the PvP [color=yellow][hint=\"Peer-to-Peer, both machines must be on the same network\"]P2P[/hint][/color] mode.[/p]


[center][img width=26]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_game-icons/mouse.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]CONTROLS[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[ul]
MOUSE - Most interactions, everything can be done just with the mouse
F - To toggle fullscreen
ESC - [b]Tap[/b] to pause, [b]Hold[/b] to close the game
[/ul]


[center][img width=26]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_game-icons/home.png[/img]  [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]TITLE SCREEN[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[center][img width=600]res://Assets/Tutorial/TitleScreen.png[/img][/center]

"
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false

[node name="Right" type="RichTextLabel" parent="TabContainer/About 1" unique_id=1560984228]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 919.0
offset_top = 56.0
offset_right = 1621.0
offset_bottom = 913.0
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[p fill]In the [b]Title Screen[/b] you will find 6 buttons, 3 big ones with 2 of them being related to game modes, 1 to quit the game, and the other 3 small ones being on the top-right side of the screen, each of them are:[/p]

[ul]
AI MODE - Clicking it will start a match against the basic AI
PVP MODE - Clicking it will open a second menu (we'll talk about it in a bit) for PvP matchmaking
QUIT - Clicking it will close the game
Sound Icon - [b]Mutes[/b] or [b]unmutes[/b] the game based on which state it currently is
Book Icon - It's the button for opening the tutorial
Info Icon - It has the credits/attribuitions to the assets providers
[/ul]


[center][img width=26]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_game-icons/multiplayer.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]PvP MODE MENU[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[center][img width=300]res://Assets/Tutorial/PvpMenu.png[/img][/center]


[p fill]Within this menu you are given 3 choices, to [b]Host[/b] a match, [b]Join[/b] a match, or to simply return to the title screen. You can also cancel your choice by clicking any of the other buttons. [color=red]But[/color], like it was mentioned before, the PvP in this game operates in a P2P basis, therefore not only both machines need to have a network connection, it must be the same network for both machines. However, you and your friend(s), don't need to be physically on the same place to play, instead you can use a VPN service like [url=https://www.radmin-vpn.com/]Radmin[/url], to create a private network, where both can connect, and the games automatic ip detection will let you play toghether.[/p]
"
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false

[node name="About 2" type="Panel" parent="TabContainer" unique_id=212691036]
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
metadata/_tab_index = 2

[node name="Label" type="Label" parent="TabContainer/About 2" unique_id=1949421483]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 1.0
offset_top = 13.0
offset_right = 856.0
offset_bottom = 151.0
theme_override_colors/font_outline_color = Color(1, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/outline_size = 16
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("2_qouqw")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 64
text = "GAMEPLAY"
horizontal_alignment = 1
vertical_alignment = 1

[node name="Left2" type="RichTextLabel" parent="TabContainer/About 2" unique_id=208147035]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 91.0
offset_top = 142.0
offset_right = 839.0
offset_bottom = 931.0
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/cards_collection.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]CARDS[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]The cards in FNAF WORLD TCG, consist of 2 types and 5 colors. The types are [b]Entity[/b] and [b]Skill[/b], with the entity cards being divided by the colors: [color=red]RED[/color], [color=green]GREEN[/color], [color=yellow]YELLOW[/color] and [color=blue]BLUE[/color], while the skill cards are colored [color=violet]PURPLE[/color].[/p]

[center][img width=100]res://Assets/Tutorial/Freddy.png[/img][/center]
[center][font_size=12]- Freddy is a entity card, of the [color=green]Green[/color] group[/font_size][/center]

[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/card_down_outline.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]ARENA[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]The Arena is where the matches will take place, weather it is against the AI or against another player, your side of the Arena can be seen on the image bellow. In it you can see the places where your cards can be placed, deck of cards, cemetery, action buttons and health. When on a match your opponents side of the Arena is basically a mirror of yours.[/p]

[center][img width=420]res://Assets/Tutorial/PlayerSide.png[/img][/center]
[center][font_size=12]- The player's side of the Arena[/font_size][/center]



"
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false

[node name="Right2" type="RichTextLabel" parent="TabContainer/About 2" unique_id=2100032076]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 919.0
offset_top = 56.0
offset_right = 1621.0
offset_bottom = 913.0
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][img width=420]res://Assets/Tutorial/Arena.png[/img][/center]
[center][font_size=12]- The Arena during a match[/font_size][/center]

[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/cards_take.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]DRAWING CARDS[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]You can draw cards by clicking on your deck. The deck is composed of 54 cards, 35 of them being entity cards, and 18 being skill cards. On the first turn, both you and the opponent will automatically draw 7 cards. After that you and your opponent can draw up to 3 cards per turn, however your hands size is limited to 7 cards at a time. Keep in mind however that if, for example, you had had 6 cards upon starting a new turn, and made your first draw, after freeing up your hand by playing a card, while it still is your turn, you may make any leftover draws.[/p]

[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/card_place.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]PLACING CARDS[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p]You can place cards by clicking them on your hand, that is as long as you have a free slot of the same color as the card you are trying to place. So you can place a entity card on each free entity slot as long as their colors match, and while it is your turn. Skill cards work similarly, the main diference being that, skill cards take action upon being placed, so after the skill finishes the card will automatically move itself to the cemitery. This allows the player to use as many skills they have in hand during their turn. Just keep in mind that aside from one skill ([color=violet]Slasher[/color]), the skills act upon entities on field, so playing these cards when there aren't opponent entities on field you'll just be wasting that skill card.[/p]"
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false

[node name="About 3" type="Panel" parent="TabContainer" unique_id=544293600]
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
metadata/_tab_index = 3

