[node name="Left2" type="RichTextLabel" parent="TabContainer/About 3" unique_id=1379232049]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 59.0
offset_top = 142.0
offset_right = 807.0
offset_bottom = 978.0
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/cards_fan.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]ATTACKING[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]Attacking can be done from the second player's turn and foward. When you can attack the button labeled ATTACK will become visible and you'll be able to perform an attack towards your opponent side of the Arena for that turn. The attack can be divided in 2 types: [b]Direct Attacks[/b], where the units directly damages a player's health points, and [b]Clash Attacks[/b], which happen when a attacking entity is being blocked by an opposing entity of the same color. On clash attacks, the entities will mutually damage each other, and in the case of their health points being expended, they will be moved to the cemitery, freeing up the slot they were occupying.[/p]

[center][img width=400]res://Assets/Tutorial/ArenaWithCards.png[/img][/center]

[center][font_size=12]- By starting an attack, Golden Freddy and Fredbear, Springtrap and Toy Bonnie, as well as Withered Bonnie and Nightmare would engage on clash attacks for being part of the same color group, while Phantom Chica would directly attack the opponents health points as she isn't being blocked by another [color=green]green[/color] entity.[/font_size][/center]

[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/book_open.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]SKILLS[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]Skills are cards that can be used to damage the opponents units or their health points without having to attack them. There are currently 6 skills in the game, they are:[/p]

[ul]
Pizza Wheel				    4th Wall
Pizza Wheel 2				Jack-O-Bomb
Mega Bite						Slasher
[/ul]									


"
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false

[node name="Right2" type="RichTextLabel" parent="TabContainer/About 3" unique_id=877449942]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 919.0
offset_top = 56.0
offset_right = 1621.0
offset_bottom = 913.0
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[p fill]Both versions of Pizza Wheel and 4th Wall are skills capable of damaging all of your opponent units, so if you want to clean up the field before launching an attack they're your go to skills. Mega Bite and Jack-O-Bomb are targeted skills, upon playing one of them, they will randomly select an opponent unit and act upon them. Finally Slasher is a skill that allows you to directly damage your opponent by instantly winning the game!, that is however, if you hit the luck 10% chance of that happening.[/p]

[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/hourglass.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]ENDING YOUR TURN[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]After you performed every action you can during your turn, you may end it by pressing the END TURN button, plan your actions accordingly, a turn ended badly may cause a swift defeat.[/p]

[center][img width=26]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_game-icons/trophy.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]WINNING or LOSING[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b] [img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_board-game-icons/skull.png[/img][/center]

[p fill]The game can end in many ways. It ends when yours or your opponent's health points reaches 0, if both players run out of cards, in which case, the one who wins is, the one with more health points, and in the case of both having the same amount of HP, it ends with a Draw.[/p]

[center][img width=18]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_game-icons/pause.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]PAUSING[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]It's also worth noting that during matches you can pause the game, in the AI mode it doesn't have any downsides, you can use the pause menu to quit a match, mute the game or read the tutorial. It is the same on the PvP mode, but with a small change, to prevent hostage keeping, your opponent (or you), will be presented with a menu of their own, in which after 20 seconds it's possible to quite the match, without settling it first. But in case of abuse of the pause menu, remember that it still is possible to quit the game by just closing it (or holding ESC), you won't lose anything.[/p]

[center][img width=26]res://Assets/Icons/kenney_game-icons/multiplayer.png[/img] [b][outline_size=2][outline_color=red]DISCONNECTING on PvP MATCHES[/outline_color][/outline_size][/b][/center]

[p fill]In case your or your opponent lose their connection during a match a menu informing of their connection loss will pop up, so that you may go back to the title screen or quit the game.[/p]"
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false

